From b3005d3dcfeffc0e097e9286e921b0597969b356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:35:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): an empty reply to a wake or after agent_send ends
 the turn quietly

A turn whose input is a message from another agent, a background process
result or a background subagent result, with no tool run yet, or whose
newest tool round was only agent_send, may now end with no text and no
tool call. Before, that took the empty-response ladder: a "you returned
an empty response, continue" nudge after tool calls, retries, then a
"no reply" error text. Models learned that ending quietly is an error
and ended such turns with a harmless tool call such as execute_code
print("ok").

The turn now ends at once with turn_exit_reason quiet_end, no further
request, and an empty assistant row that closes the transcript. The
gateway delivers nothing for it: no retry hint, no no-response text.
Any other empty reply (a user's message, a wake after other tools) takes
the ladder as before.
---
